    sections: [{ heading: 'Use the relevant food authority', paragraphs: ['Official food-business guidance covers safety, hygiene and registration and points to different national arrangements. Check the jurisdiction and actual operating activity. Do not treat a general guide or a rating for one premises as proof that every proposed site or service is compliant.'], source: 'food' }, { heading: 'Substitution has contractual consequences', paragraphs: ['Record which ingredients or supply routes can change, who checks dietary implications and who tells the client. A backup supplier is not a complete continuity plan if prices, availability and permitted substitutions are unconfirmed. Keep specialist food-safety sign-off separate from writing review.'] }],
    fieldHelp: ['Reference service windows, locations and specification.', 'Link the relevant operating system and review owner.', 'Identify controlled allergen processes, not blanket assurances.', 'Map shifts and confirmed cover.', 'Track supply dependencies and authorised alternatives.', 'Use attributable dated evidence with its site scope.'],
